WEBVTT

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:07.440
That day...

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:12.280
On orders from up top, I was attached in a supporting role to...

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.280
Him.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.120
Togo, in Derry, Northern Ireland.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.540
The target was an executive of a hostile organization.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:21.830
Mac Guinness.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.750
Togo entered the prone shooting position at sunset,

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.960
and remained motionless through the night.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.050
Mac Guinness's room was 800 meters away.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.600
Furthermore, the wind was strong that night.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.890
He remained motionless that way,

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.020
three hours without moving.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.150
The cold concrete must have been painful.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:52.240
I thought it was impossible.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:58.700
Did you do it?

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:00.330
Yes.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.050
To stare at a room for three hours.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.720
and, to kill with just one bullet.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:19.430
That night...

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.220
Togo and I got married, because I don't believe in premarital sexual relations.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:23.980
It seemed...

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:28.190
I fell captive to the charm of the bloody fragrance of his whole body.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:06.890
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.020
wondering what I should do right now.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:17.490
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:22.030
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:27.660
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:33.090
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:37.550
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:43.850
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:48.140
Oh someday - one of these days

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:53.230
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:59.320
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:04.910
depend on me for your repairs.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.290
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:15.500
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:19.800
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:25.850
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:37.780
Catherine the Cold-Blooded

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.880
Those cowardly executives.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:57.670
I cannot forgive them!

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.710
What is this pacifist doctrine?

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:03.050
The reason we split off from the former organization

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:06.260
was because we could not agree with that line!

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.100
Calm down Pamela, times have changed.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.140
Self-government has returned.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.730
Compared to before, there are a lot more smiles in this town.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:18.650
Smiles?

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.440
Times have changed?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.150
You're the one who has changed, Catherine!

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.780
I have no business with domesticated smiles.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.330
Unification comes by force of arms!

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.040
This was our purpose, wasn't it?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:32.910
Catherine?!

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.080
We should resume fighting now.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:41.630
I will not waste the blood that our ancestors and comrades have shed!

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.510
You coward. Wake up!

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.430
Here is your gun.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:53.890
Do you need a ride?

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:56.230
Thanks, but no thanks.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.400
I can still take care of myself.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.150
She's changed...

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.820
Catherine the Cold-Hearted.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.120
Cold-Hearted?

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:08.990
Yeah.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:14.540
Cruel and ruthless. It's as if she has no human feelings in her.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.920
Well, used to have.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.120
No way.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.000
Cowardly Catherine, who cannot even look Pamela in the eye?

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.460
Aye, Catherine the Cold-Hearted.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.840
She was a true terrorist through and through.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:35.940
Once, we sneaked into a fashionable hotel in London.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.110
It was a fashionable party for wealthy business leaders.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:42.440
The purpose was to make them hear our guiding principles.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:57.370
We declare the continuance of the armed struggle, in front of you overweight English pigs!

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.960
Hey, give it a rest you old-fashioned terrorists!

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:08.010
Who supports you in this day and age?

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.180
Go back to the small grey island where you were born!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:21.650
I cannot forgive someone who insults our dead comrades.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.360
Please play.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.820
The song is Chopin's Polonaise.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:33.870
Only that tune filled with ethnic pride is suitable for this hall.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:48.420
Catherine fluently recited our manifesto to a background of polonaise.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.550
Her voice full of confidence.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.650
I will do away with these dogs. Get out of here!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.540
She's not a woman who belongs under Pamela.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.580
Then why?

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:19.580
Who knows?

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.580
Something happened.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:40.890
Mister Togo.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:46.520
Have you checked the three million dollars we transferred to the Swiss Bank?

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.740
I am here, as we agreed.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.990
That question is pointless.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:52.860
I see.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.700
Then let me get to the point right away.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:01.250
The target is this woman in Northern Ireland.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:13.550
As it turned out, our armed struggle did not solve anything.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:19.270
I have lived with the organization, therefore I understand it best.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.180
But Pamela is different.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:25.100
Pamela does not agree with the top's decision.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.270
The discussion seems to have broken down.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:29.440
Aye...

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:34.240
After that, she shut herself up in that building.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:39.290
She's surrounding herself with companions who share her violent standpoint.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.660
Pamela is a very cautious person, Charlie.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:47.040
She suspects that one day you could be her enemy.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:51.710
In this situation, only you can get through to her.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:56.050
You've been in this fight together from childhood.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:01.390
Please get her to accept discussion again, somehow.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.770
We are comrades.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.230
If we speak from our heart, we can surely understand each other.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.070
Tell her in your own words.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.110
Please do this favour for me, Catherine.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:15.610
All right.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.710
Yes?

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.550
Seems like your guest has left.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:33.460
Pamela!

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.970
I hope you don't think that I can be at the beck and call of such cowardly people.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.180
I'll show you something nice.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:42.850
Look outside your window.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:50.110
Your guest, Charlie, is going home.

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:51.400
What about Charlie?

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:52.860
He is going to get in his car.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:55.360
No...

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.530
It's a white car.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:59.070
Don't do it, Pamela!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:14.090
Doesn't this bring back memories, Catherine?

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:16.510
We will always be comrades.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:30.520
It's a shame that you waste your skill by being a woman.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:32.360
What do you want?

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.360
Pamela wants to see you.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:37.030
Tell her that I'll see her when I want to see her.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.610
Pamela can sit tight.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.740
You're not usually this bold.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.750
Is it true, Jack?

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:49.040
Did Catherine say that?

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:51.210
It's true Pamela.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:54.500
She wasn't the usual timid Catherine.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:55.840
What happened?

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:57.590
I don't know.

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.130
You don't need to see Catherine?

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:03.600
She said she'll come when she's ready, didn't she?

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:05.350
That's enough.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:06.680
Understood.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:12.770
I don't believe it.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:15.770
After all this time, you defy me?

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:20.030
Sure, you used to be the hero of our group.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:24.370
You were a person of action, daring. Never scared of being killed on the job.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.330
All of our leaders praised you.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:35.210
In contrast, I was always inconspicuous, cautious. Crawling around drains like a rat, planting bombs.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:39.720
Feared by people, but never in the limelight.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:41.380
Now what's this?

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:47.350
I don't know what happened, but now she's just a toothless coward without any claws.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:52.190
It's fine by me that you have woken up, but I will not forgive you if you turn against me.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:52.980
Catherine.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:55.060
I'll never forgive you.

00:11:55.770 --> 00:12:00.360
I cannot forgive you. How can you kill Charlie like some worthless vermin? He was my dead father's best friend.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:02.280
What's more...

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:07.950
If I leave Pamela by herself, she will eventually continue terrorist bombings.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.790
I cannot let things stand.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.150
Togo.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:43.490
It's been a while.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:46.450
I never expected to see you again.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.200
Let me hear your business.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:53.620
Can we go someplace more relaxing? If that's all right by you.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.470
It reminds me of the past.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.140
I was waiting for this day for a long time.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:56.480
Yes...

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:58.400
Always waiting.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.560
Let me hear your business.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:03.980
Sorry I made you waste your time.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:05.650
You see...

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:16.250
Now, Pamela will not even take one step out of the building,

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.250
which is guarded by her armed comrades.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:24.670
She will probably keep to herself until there is no more opposition left in the organization.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:27.380
And yet...

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:32.010
We have fought together since childhood.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.250
We are practically family.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:04.460
I cannot do it.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:09.840
I cannot prepare your payment right now.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:13.050
But I will definitely do it!

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:15.680
Please, Togo.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:20.140
Can you still approach her?

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:25.070
Yes, after a stringent body check.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.490
Alright. I accept.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:31.200
Thank you, Togo.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:44.000
This place has been a battlefield since before I was born.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:49.010
This grey town only exists for fighting.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:54.010
For someone once called cold-hearted, you have become quite sentimental.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:55.510
It doesn't suit me?

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:00.060
Yes, I have changed.

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:03.940
That night, four years after I first met you.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:07.520
It was a snowy day.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:12.490
At that time, many of my comrades would stay at my house.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.780
Sometimes we would prepare explosives there.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:16.830
Joey?

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:19.080
Joey, where are you?

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:21.040
Oh no!

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:26.540
Joey! I told you not to go into that room!

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:33.930
That day...

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:37.550
Catherine McCall, the cold hearted, died.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:39.770
I...

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:41.680
Killed Joey.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.480
That boy...

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:49.940
He had black hair, and stone black eyes. Just like you.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:56.370
Sorry, this story has nothing to do with you.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:19.890
Whenever Pamela is in that room, the blackout curtains are always closed.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:24.560
When she meets someone at night, she will use that room. Without exception.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:29.520
The curtains are closed, but Pamela will not approach the window.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:35.360
What I'm saying is, I want you to snipe her behind the curtain.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:41.620
In order to snipe an invisible target, I will guide her to the sniping point.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.500
Point of the target?

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:45.790
The right side of the window.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.330
On top of the object, inside the circle.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.130
I will bring her to it.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:53.340
It's the height of Pamela's head.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:58.970
However, after the curtain's closed, you will have to shoot from image memory.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:04.020
You are sure that's the height of the target's head?

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:04.850
Yes.

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:10.060
Your extraordinary shooting skill can pull this off, right?

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.660
Can you hear me, Duke?

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.910
When Pamela stands in this position, I will give the signal.

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:36.880
You haven't contacted me in a while. I thought you might have run away somewhere.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:38.970
I'm not going anywhere.

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:41.890
I don't belong anywhere.

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:45.350
Except this town. Just like you.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:57.860
Please don't lump me together with a coward like yourself.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:03.080
So, you said you wanted to give me something. What is it?

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:07.370
The schedule of the moderates.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.750
You want them dead, no?

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:13.920
Is this supposed to be a gift?

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.930
What are you trying to pull,

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:23.260
Catherine?

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:25.720
What are you saying?

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:31.900
I know you. That face means you're up to no good.

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:35.110
You know, we have been comrades for many years.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:43.370
And I just got some disturbing information just now.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:50.250
They said English Intelligence has sent an assassin to kill me.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:53.330
No wonder I'm so cautious.

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.750
An assassin?

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:56.340
Who do you think?

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:59.090
It's Golgo 13.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:03.760
Come to think of it, you have teamed up with him before.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:07.060
I don't need payment.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:10.600
Can you still approach Pamela?

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:13.650
Understood. I will do this.

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:19.530
So, I wasn't the only one to ask.

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.700
Catherine, tell me!

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:26.450
Just what are you trying to pull?

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:31.460
Why did you come here?

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:33.830
Answer me!

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:39.210
Pamela, are you scared of me?

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:43.220
What can you do without a weapon?

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.930
Is that what you think, Pamela?

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:50.270
I have many sympathizers.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:54.020
Body checks are not always so thorough.

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:15.920
As expected Togo...

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:20.920
Determining the location of the target by the muzzle flash through the curtain.

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:24.550
I'm sorry, Pamela.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.930
My only friend...

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:29.300
Sniped from outside?

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:30.140
I'm sorry.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.940
The curtain is closed, how can a hidden person be sniped?

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:43.490
What kind of person could do this?

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:46.490
Hey, what's this?

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:45.840
I enjoyed the little things.

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:53.050
I loved when you gave me a flower every day

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:59.140
instead of just one big bouquet

00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:03.980
of flowers.

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:11.620
It was like a romance novel.

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:16.200
Surely someday... just kidding.

00:23:16.490 --> 00:23:19.580
I had a dream.

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:25.300
Your face shined eternally.

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:31.890
Because I think of you all the time.

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:37.430
I'm sorry, but on a lonely night like this

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:43.940
I'm remembering you, but

00:23:44.110 --> 00:23:48.530
I won't cry like I did that day.

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:51.700
I won't.

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:05.040
People suddenly attack Golgo.

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:10.010
Fearless, due to the shock of an accident.

00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:18.010
Golgo contacts a boy and sells information to discover the man behind them.

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:21.140
Golgo challenges the invisible enemy.

00:24:21.770 --> 00:24:23.730
Next time, on Golgo's Baby:

00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:27.360
Fearless

00:24:23.730 --> 00:24:24.730
Fearless

00:24:25.400 --> 00:24:28.980
Don't stand behind him if you value your life.
